import collections, json
from common import ROOT, save
base=ROOT/'E5';rows=json.loads((base/'results.json').read_text())['fixtures']
known=[r for r in rows if 'known_actual_Android_getter_outcome' in r];groups={}
for row in rows:
 a=row['aliases'][0];key=a['phase']+'/'+a['variant'];entry=groups.setdefault(key,{'fixtures':0,'S':collections.Counter(),'D':collections.Counter()});entry['fixtures']+=1
 entry['S'][row['report']['STRUCTURAL']['status']]+=1;entry['D'][row['report']['DECODER_COMPATIBILITY']['status']]+=1
external=[]
for row in rows:
 for alias in row['aliases']:
  if alias['phase']!='E4_external':continue
  frozen=alias['frozen_D'];new=row['report']['DECODER_COMPATIBILITY']['status']
  expected='INCOMPATIBLE' if isinstance(frozen,list) and any(c['status']=='FAIL' for c in frozen) else 'COMPATIBLE_PRECONDITIONS' if isinstance(frozen,list) else 'INAPPLICABLE_NO_SELECTED_GETTER'
  external.append({'component':row['model_sha256'],'frozen_expected':expected,'new':new,'agrees':expected==new})
summary={'distinct_artifact_fixtures':len(rows),'structural_counts':dict(collections.Counter(x['report']['STRUCTURAL']['status'] for x in rows)),
 'decoder_counts':dict(collections.Counter(x['report']['DECODER_COMPATIBILITY']['status'] for x in rows)),
 'semantic_counts':dict(collections.Counter(x['report']['REFERENCE_BACKED_SEMANTIC']['status'] for x in rows)),
 'controller_errors':sum('controller_error' in x['report'] for x in rows),'known_successfully_executed_Android_artifact_conditions':sum(x['known_actual_Android_getter_outcome']=='PASS' for x in known),
 'incorrect_rejections_of_those_conditions':sum(x.get('incorrect_rejection_of_successfully_executed_path',False) for x in known),'known_getter_failure_flagged':all(x.get('preflight_flags_known_getter_failure') for x in known if x['known_actual_Android_getter_outcome']=='FAIL'),
 'external_frozen_comparison':external,'group_counts':groups,
 'limits':['No independently labeled precision/recall dataset.','Reference comparison feature not independently semantically validated.','Three dynamic-signature Gesture fixtures intentionally abstain, including one previously failing isolated decoder.','Compilation and unsupported-output warnings remain separate official diagnostics.']}
save(base/'summary.json',summary)
lines=['# E5 results','', f"The pre-flight command was applied to {len(rows)} byte-distinct fixtures; aliases to development, E1/E2 and external phases are retained. These are not independent models.",'', '| Condition group (first alias) | Fixtures | Structural results | Decoder results |','|---|---:|---|---|']
for key,value in groups.items():lines.append(f"| {key} | {value['fixtures']} | {dict(value['S'])} | {dict(value['D'])} |")
lines+=['','## Detection and abstention','', 'S accepts 52 fixtures, rejects the 11 count-reduction controls using the existing official population check, and abstains on two no-metadata originals. D flags 27 selected category paths, finds eight compatible under its stated static preconditions, marks 14 inapplicable, and abstains on three dynamic-signature Gesture fixtures. Eleven structurally rejected fixtures do not reach D. All 65 semantic judgments abstain because no independently supplied artifact-tied semantic reference is provided.','', 'The dynamic-signature abstention is deliberately more conservative than the earlier isolated Gesture probes at concrete shape [1,8]. It includes the 7-label mutant whose isolated decoder already failed. This is a disclosed limit; the pre-flight command does not claim to detect every previously observed failure. The 15 external scope-filtered outcomes agree with the frozen E4 results; this is implementation agreement, not detector accuracy.','', f"Among {summary['known_successfully_executed_Android_artifact_conditions']} distinct artifact conditions with actual successful E1/E2 Android getters, the command makes {summary['incorrect_rejections_of_those_conditions']} incompatible/structural-rejection judgments. The real EfficientNet 999-label getter failure is flagged after generation and before compilation/loading/inference. Permutation is compatible under D, with semantic abstention.",'', 'Exact diagnostic: “Generated category getter getProbabilityAsCategoryList for output 0 is incompatible with the selected TensorLabel path because selected axis 1 has size 1000, which differs from label count 999.”','', '## Existing checks and earliest failures','', 'The official MetadataPopulator already rejects count reductions. TensorLabel already throws at the failing generated getter; Task ImageClassifier already rejects the same deletion during initialization. E5 collects and moves the selected Java path precondition to pre-flight. For uncompilable wrappers, javac is already the first observed rejection; a D finding does not establish a prevented runtime failure there. Unsupported non-RGB fallback warnings remain visible.','', 'The command emits separate STRUCTURAL, REFERENCE_BACKED_SEMANTIC, DECODER_COMPATIBILITY, PRESERVATION and UNKNOWN_ABSTAIN sections. It parses actual tensor and associated-file bindings and the understood default postprocessor. It makes no “model invalid” statement. Optional reference comparison verifies supplied bytes/digests and compares a supplied contract; source interpretation and artifact linkage require human verification, and this feature has no independently labeled semantic evaluation here.','', 'CLI exits 2 for a demonstrated selected-contract incompatibility or official structural rejection, 3 for tool/generation errors, and otherwise 0 while retaining explicit abstentions. Exit 0 is not universal correctness. Compilation and inference are not performed by this static command.','', '## Usage','', '```bash','PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 /workspace/hand-contract-repro/.venv/bin/python scripts/preflight.py E1/variants/label_deletion/model.tflite --evidence-dir /tmp/new-preflight-evidence','```','', 'The evidence directory must be new; old results are never overwritten. Exact code, generated sources, logs, aliases and machine results are under E5/.','']
(ROOT/'EXPERIMENT_E5_RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines));print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in summary.items() if k not in ['group_counts','external_frozen_comparison']},indent=2))
